item.content:encoded:
&lt;p&gt;Zhihu (知乎) is China's largest Q&amp;amp;A site, and its hot list (知乎热榜) is one of the best real-time signals of what people in China are debating right now. The problem: it's in Chinese, it changes every few minutes, and there is no official public API. In this tutorial you will pull the hot list into Python, in English, in about 15 lines of code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You will get, for each question:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rank, title and excerpt (plus English translations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heat score (热度) and number of answers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The question URL and the time it was scraped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Full disclosure: I built the scraper used here. It reads Zhihu's public hot list, so you don't need a Zhihu account, a login or a Chinese phone number.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Setup (2 minutes)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a free account at &lt;a href="https://apify.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;apify.com&lt;/a&gt;. The free plan includes monthly credits, enough to follow this tutorial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Copy your API token from &lt;strong&gt;Settings → API &amp;amp; Integrations&lt;/strong&gt; in the &lt;a href="https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Apify Console&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install the client and save the token as an environment variable:
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pip install &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"apify-client&amp;gt;=3"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;APIFY_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"your_token_here"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Get today's hot list, in English
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;apify_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"APIFY_TOKEN"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"neronbaez/zhihu-hot-list-scraper"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"maxItemsPerPlatform"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# top 10 questions of the hot list&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"translateToEnglish"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;     &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# adds titleEn / excerptEn&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;questions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;default_dataset_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;iterate_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;questions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'#{q["rank"]:&amp;gt;2} | {q["heat"]:&amp;gt;9,} heat | {q.get("answers", 0):&amp;gt;5} answers | '&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'{q.get("titleEn") or q["title"]}'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is the real output from a run on November 25, 2026 (first 5 lines):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# 1 | 8,230,000 heat |    98 answers | The launch of the Shenzhou 24 manned spacecraft was a complete success. The Chinese Space Station welcomed its first foreign astronaut. What other highlights are there in this launch mission?
# 2 | 4,640,000 heat |   175 answers | Young people are beginning to persuade their parents to sell their vacant houses in the county and exchange them for cash to collect interest. Is it necessary to keep a house that has been vacant for many years?
# 3 | 2,400,000 heat |   192 answers | The AI short drama "Ugly Fox" sparked a lot of discussion after it became popular. What is the core reason why it can hit the audience?
# 4 | 2,290,000 heat |    28 answers | Trump publicly mentioned a Chinese dish with a beautiful "hat" and said it was delicious but couldn't name it. Which dish could it be?
# 5 | 2,180,000 heat |   175 answers | Why do I think Mr. Bean's performance is very vulgar and childish and not funny at all? Is it the difference between Chinese and Western cultures?
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The titles are machine translations of the original Zhihu questions. Each question comes back as a JSON object like this one (trimmed, real data):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"trend"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"platform"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"zhihu"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"神舟二十四号载人飞船发射取得圆满成功，中国空间站迎来首位外籍航天员，此次发射任务还有哪些看点？"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"heat"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8230000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"heatText"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"823 万热度"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"answers"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;98&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"url"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.zhihu.com/question/2108654680351797564"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"rank"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Find the open conversations: hot but under-answered
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A question with huge heat and few answers is a conversation that is still open. For a brand, a journalist or a creator, that is where a good answer gets the most attention.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;questions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"heatPerAnswer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"heat"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"answers"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;open_topics&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;sorted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;questions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;lambda&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"heatPerAnswer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;reverse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Hot but under-answered:"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;open_topics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'  {q["heatPerAnswer"]:&amp;gt;10,.0f} heat/answer | {q.get("titleEn") or q["title"]}'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Real output from the same run:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Hot but under-answered:
83,980 heat/answer | The launch of the Shenzhou 24 manned spacecraft was a complete success. The Chinese Space Station welcomed its first foreign astronaut. What other highlights are there in this launch mission?
81,786 heat/answer | Trump publicly mentioned a Chinese dish with a beautiful "hat" and said it was delicious but couldn't name it. Which dish could it be?
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Going further
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track it over time.&lt;/strong&gt; The hot list changes all day. Schedule the Actor every hour in Apify (Schedules tab) and save each run: you'll see which topics rise, how long they stay and how fast they die.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compare platforms.&lt;/strong&gt; The &lt;a href="https://apify.com/neronbaez/china-trending-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;China Trending Topics&lt;/a&gt; Actor puts Zhihu, Weibo, Baidu, Bilibili and Douyin trends together and detects topics trending on several platforms at once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cost.&lt;/strong&gt; You pay per result: $0.001 per hot question, so the full top 50 costs $0.05. Translation to English is included at no extra cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Wrap-up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You now have China's live conversation as data, in English. You can also run the &lt;a href="https://apify.com/neronbaez/zhihu-hot-list-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Zhihu Hot List Scraper&lt;/a&gt; from the browser without code and export to CSV or Excel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you need a field or filter it doesn't have, open an issue on the Actor page and I'll add it. What would you track first? Tell me in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I recently needed a way to sell small digital downloads from a static GitHub Pages site without adding a conventional backend, merchant account, database, or card processor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The store now has a working Lightning checkout built from three pieces:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a static HTML form&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a Netlify Function that owns prices and creates invoices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://openreceive.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;OpenReceive&lt;/a&gt; connected to a receive-only Nostr Wallet Connect (NWC) wallet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The live checkout is used for the &lt;a href="https://secondwindmc.github.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;SecondWindMC digital products store&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://secondwindmc.github.io/circuit-ui-sfx.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Circuit UI SFX pack&lt;/a&gt;. This article is the implementation pattern and the important caveats.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The shape of the checkout
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The static page does not mint invoices in the browser. It only submits a product code:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"https://example.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/lightning"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"post"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"hidden"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"product"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"sound-pack-v1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Pay by Lightning&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The serverless function owns the catalog:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'sound-pack-v1'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Circuit UI SFX Vol. 1'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'6.99'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That matters because the payer must never be trusted to choose the amount.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The function then creates an OpenReceive checkout:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;createOpenReceive&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@openreceive/node'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;svc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createOpenReceive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;receive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'nwc'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;connectionString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;NWC_URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;svc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createCheckout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;reference&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;randomUUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'USD'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;memo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Example store ${product.name}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;itemCode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;expirySeconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;OpenReceive returns the payment hash, BOLT11 invoice, amount in millisatoshis, creation time, expiry, and fiat quote. The function renders those as a QR code plus a copyable invoice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why receive-only NWC is useful
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The wallet connection is the dangerous secret in this design, so the wallet is connected through a receive-only NWC code. In my case the vault is hosted by &lt;a href="https://rizful.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Rizful&lt;/a&gt;. The code can create invoices and inspect incoming transactions, but it is not supposed to spend funds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is a useful least-privilege boundary for a serverless checkout. It is not self-custody: the hosted wallet is still custodial until funds are withdrawn. Treat it as operational cash, not long-term cold storage, and keep withdrawal hygiene separate from checkout code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Payment status is not a client claim
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A stateless static store still needs some way to connect a browser session back to the invoice it created. I used a short signed receipt containing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;itemCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;paymentHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;createdAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;reference&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The receipt is HMAC-signed with a server-side secret. It is not proof of payment. It only prevents casual tampering with the product code and payment hash while the browser polls for status.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The important verification still happens server-side:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checks&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;svc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reconcilePayments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;attempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;paymentHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;createdAt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;maxPages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;checks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;find&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;paymentHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;paymentHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'settled'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;paymentPendingPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;deliverZip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That order is deliberate:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;verify the signed receipt,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ask the wallet for the payment state,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;deliver only after the wallet reports settlement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Delivery in a serverless response
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Large zip files can run into synchronous serverless response limits. The first version of this system hit exactly that problem, so the delivery page downloads large archives in verified chunks and reassembles them in the browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Small archives can be returned directly. Large archives are chunked; each chunk is still gated by the same server-side payment verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What this pattern is good for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a pragmatic fit for low-friction digital downloads:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;static marketing site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fixed catalog and fixed prices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no customer accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;automatic delivery after settlement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;minimal infrastructure beyond serverless functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OpenReceive also supports optional swap providers for USDT, USDC, SOL, and ETH, converted into BTC over Lightning in the merchant wallet. Asset and network availability depends on the configured provider. I have not enabled swaps yet because short/late swap payments introduce refund responsibilities that need a more deliberate UI and operational process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it is not
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is not a replacement for a real ecommerce order system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A store with customer accounts, inventory, taxes, partial payments, subscriptions, refund workflows, or fulfillment reconciliation should use durable order and payment-attempt rows. OpenReceive's normal integrations are designed around that stronger model. The HMAC receipt approach here is intentionally narrow: it is for a tiny fixed digital-download catalog where every checkout attempt can be re-verified against the wallet before delivery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Current production verification
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The deployed checkout has been verified up to the payment step:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;it creates real Lightning invoices and QR checkout pages,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;unpaid invoices correctly remain pending,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;invalid receipts are rejected,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;unpaid delivery attempts do not expose the zip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I am not claiming a completed end-to-end settled-payment delivery until a real payment is observed. The checkout is live at &lt;a href="https://secondwindmc.github.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;secondwindmc.github.io&lt;/a&gt; if you want to inspect the buyer-facing flow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A live trade feed looks easy to poll: call it, print what comes back, sleep, repeat. It goes wrong in three quiet ways. You miss trades between two calls, you count the same trade twice, or you restart the script and lose your place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post builds a small poller in Python that avoids all three, using the public &lt;code&gt;copytop&lt;/code&gt; package from PyPI and the free copy.top trades feed. It keeps a cursor, drops duplicates by key, saves its place in a file so a crash costs nothing, and backs off when the API answers with an error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Disclosure: I am the founder of copy.top. copy.top is independent and not affiliated with pumpfun or fomo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Setup
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install copytop
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The package is standard library only and needs no key. I tested with copytop 0.1.0 on Python 3.14.5. The feed is read-only: nothing here places an order.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two methods matter. &lt;code&gt;Client().trades(since=..., limit=...)&lt;/code&gt; calls the live tape and returns &lt;code&gt;{"cursor": ..., "trades": [...]}&lt;/code&gt;, newest first. The client also retries on its own, but I turn that off below (&lt;code&gt;max_retries=0&lt;/code&gt;) so the backoff is ours and visible. The docstring of &lt;code&gt;trades&lt;/code&gt; says the tape keeps the latest 30 trades and tells you to poll at least once a minute to miss none. That sentence drives the whole design.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why a cursor and not a timestamp
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The obvious way to ask for "only new trades" is to remember the time of your last call and pass it as &lt;code&gt;since&lt;/code&gt;. It fails in two places.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your clock is not the server's clock.&lt;/strong&gt; If your machine runs 3 seconds ahead, trades from the last 3 seconds are skipped on every call. If it runs behind, you get repeats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The time of your call is not the time of the data.&lt;/strong&gt; A trade can reach the feed after you asked. A timestamp taken when you called already sits past it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A cursor sidesteps both. The server hands back a value, and you give it back untouched on the next call. In this feed the cursor is an ISO time, but it is the time of the newest trade the server returned, not a time you read on your own machine. You never compare it with your clock. If a call returns nothing new, you keep the cursor you had.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What the feed actually returns
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I called it once with &lt;code&gt;limit=3&lt;/code&gt; before writing the code, to see the shape. A trade is a small object with &lt;code&gt;at&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;handle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;side&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;chain&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;token&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;symbol&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;usd&lt;/code&gt;. One of the three, trimmed:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"at"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-11-25T23:12:07.639Z"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"handle"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pf_0095f58aa0c5"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"side"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"buy"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"chain"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"solana"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"symbol"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"COUSIN"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"usd"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;There is no trade id. That changes the de-duplication step: the identity of a trade has to be built from its own fields. I use the time, the trader's handle, the side and the token address. Two trades that agree on all four in the same millisecond would be merged, which is a risk I accept for a feed with no better key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The poller
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Short on purpose. It has four jobs, each in one place: &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; retries with backoff, &lt;code&gt;poll_once&lt;/code&gt; de-duplicates and advances the cursor, &lt;code&gt;save_state&lt;/code&gt; writes the file, &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; loops.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# poller.py&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;__future__&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;annotations&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sys&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pathlib&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Path&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;typing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Callable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TypedDict&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;copytop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CopyTopError&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_FILE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"cursor.json"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="no"&gt;INTERVAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;60.0&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# one call a minute, never faster&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="no"&gt;MAX_SEEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;200&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# keys remembered for de-duplication&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trade&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TypedDict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;handle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;side&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;symbol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;usd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;State&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TypedDict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;cursor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;seen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trade&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# The feed has no trade id, so the identity of a trade is its own fields.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"{t['at']}|{t['handle']}|{t['side']}|{t['token']}"&lt;/span&gt;


