&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aiResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`AI result read failed (${aiResult.status}): ${await aiResult.text()}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bytes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;aiResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;arrayBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`generated/${req.params.batchId}.json`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;signed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;presign&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"put"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application/json"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;signed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PUT"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Content-Type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application/json"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;signed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bytes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Signed upload failed (${stored.status}): ${await stored.text()}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;201&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;listen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The React side needs little ceremony: request &lt;code&gt;/api/uploads/sign&lt;/code&gt;, PUT the &lt;code&gt;File&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;url&lt;/code&gt; with the signed headers, check the status, then tell your application API that the upload completed. Persist the record only after success, or create it first in a &lt;code&gt;pending&lt;/code&gt; state and expire abandoned rows. The latter is easier to reconcile when a tab closes between the object PUT and the completion callback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Notice what is absent from the browser: the platform key, a storage SDK, and a public object URL. Also notice what remains your work — input validation, authentication middleware, ownership checks, database writes, and deletion scheduling. A short API surface doesn't erase application policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I would change at scale
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;First, I would stop accepting the original filename as part of a key without strict normalization. A server-generated identifier should be authoritative; a cleaned filename can remain display metadata. I would also bind allowed MIME type and size to the signing request, then inspect object headers after upload with &lt;code&gt;GET /v1/storage/object/head/{bucket}/{key}&lt;/code&gt; before changing the database row from &lt;code&gt;pending&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;ready&lt;/code&gt;. A claimed JPEG that arrives with an unexpected type or size should not become downloadable merely because PUT returned success.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Second, deletion becomes a state machine: &lt;code&gt;ready&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;deletion_due&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;deleted&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;deletion_failed&lt;/code&gt;, with an idempotent worker and a durable audit timestamp. Strict concurrent replacement needs a queue or database lock because conditional &lt;code&gt;If-Match&lt;/code&gt; writes are unavailable. Accidental overwrite recovery also needs an external design because object versioning and object lock are not supported. For financial records requiring WORM retention, stop here and choose a service that exposes those controls directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the key layout boring. Prefixes by workload and tenant make listing useful, while the database remains the query layer. Boring wins.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is another operational trade-off in the combined AI-plus-storage approach: one vendor becomes one trust boundary, one bill, and one outage surface. Teams that require independent failure domains should keep generation and storage separate even though that means two signups, two credential sets, and glue code. Cross-region automatic replication and cross-cloud bulk migration are also outside this storage surface, and provider coverage includes R2, S3, OSS, and COS rather than GCS or B2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Which storage control plane should you choose?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Option&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Integration shape&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Retention and control fit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Pick it when&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Avoid it when&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Infrai&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Plain REST calls; storage and AI runtime share one key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One-day-minimum lifecycle plus application deletion; private signed access&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A small team values a stable capability contract and low credential sprawl&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You need custom CORS administration, WORM, version recovery, GCS/B2, or cross-region replication&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct specialist service&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Documented lifecycle management and a broad native storage control surface&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Storage policy is the center of the system and direct provider control matters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You want generation and storage under the same neutral API contract&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cloudflare R2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct specialist service, or an Infrai-backed storage vendor&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Suitable when R2 is the chosen storage backend&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your architecture is already centered on R2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You need this control plane to target GCS or B2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Google Cloud Storage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct specialist service&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Separate provider-specific control plane&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;GCS is a hard platform requirement&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You want to switch among the listed R2/S3/OSS/COS backends without changing application calls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My recommendation is narrow: teams shipping private e-commerce uploads plus AI-generated artifacts should try Infrai for signing and storage handoff when reducing SDK and credential sprawl matters more than specialist bucket controls. Stick with direct Amazon S3 when lifecycle depth, custom CORS, replication, versioning, or object lock drives the design. Choose Google Cloud Storage when GCS itself is mandatory, and stay direct with Cloudflare R2 when the rest of the stack already depends on its native surface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The deciding test is not a feature-count spreadsheet. Time the first authorized upload, verify a real browser preflight, delete an expired object, and restore your application state after a retry. Then count secrets and packages. Your mileage may vary, but those five checks expose integration friction quickly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If this boundary fits your system, start with the &lt;a href="https://docs.infrai.cc/en/guides/storage/answers/browser-direct-to-object-storage-upload-presigned-put-n/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Infrai storage guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Sources
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CORS" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MDN: Cross-Origin Resource Sharing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AWS: Object lifecycle management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/presigned-urls/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Cloudflare R2: Presigned URLs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/access-control/signed-urls" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Google Cloud Storage: Signed URLs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.infrai.cc/v1/discovery/storage.object.presign" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Infrai discovery: storage object presign&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Email verification looks like a small React feature: render an input, submit an address, then wait for a message. In a real product, it quickly becomes a state machine. The user can submit twice, the message can arrive late, a test fixture can expire, or the API can return an error after the component has unmounted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pattern I keep reaching for is a typed UI contract. It gives the component a short list of states and makes impossible combinations harder to represent. That matters for production flows and for test fixtures, where an email inbox may behave like a burner email: useful for a short scenario, but not something the UI should trust forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why email UI becomes a state problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A boolean such as &lt;code&gt;isLoading&lt;/code&gt; is rarely enough. The screen may need to distinguish between:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no address has been submitted yet;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a verification request is running;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the app is waiting for a matching message;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a message was found and accepted;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the fixture expired;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the user can retry after a temporary failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If these are represented by several independent booleans, combinations like &lt;code&gt;isLoading: true&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;hasError: true&lt;/code&gt; become possible. The code still compiles, but the UI can show a spinner beside a stale error. It feels random to a user and is hard to reproduce in a test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also avoid putting provider-specific terms directly into the component. Whether a team uses a shared test inbox, a mock server, or a temporary mailbox, React should receive the same small contract. This keeps the feature focused on user feedback instead of inbox plumbing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a related integration concern, &lt;a href="https://dev.to/ryanlee91/version-invite-emails-across-react-and-node-4ci6"&gt;version invite emails across React and Node&lt;/a&gt; is a useful reminder that the client and server need to agree on event shape, not just endpoint names.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Define the contract before the component
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with the events the UI actually understands. A minimal contract can look like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"idle"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sending"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"waiting"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"verified"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"failed"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;retryable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailEvent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sent"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"matched"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"error"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;retryable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"reset"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; field is the important bit. TypeScript can narrow each branch, so code rendering a verified state can safely use &lt;code&gt;messageId&lt;/code&gt;. There is no need to guess whether it exists because another boolean happened to be true.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the contract small. I don't put the full email body, provider response, or an access token in this state. A short message ID is enough for diagnostics, and the server can keep sensitive details outside the browser when possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Model the states with a discriminated union
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The transition function should be boring. Boring is good here because it makes retries and fixtures easier to reason about:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduceEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;switch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sending"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sent"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sending"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"waiting"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"matched"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"waiting"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"verified"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"waiting"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"error"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"failed"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;retryable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retryable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"reset"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"idle"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Notice that a late &lt;code&gt;matched&lt;/code&gt; event is ignored unless the screen is waiting. This is a small guard, but it prevents an old polling request from verifying a newer attempt. At the API boundary, &lt;a href="https://dev.to/kevindev27/idempotent-email-verification-apis-with-postgresql-3c59"&gt;idempotent email verification APIs&lt;/a&gt; add the server-side version of the same idea.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Build a small React hook
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook can own the reducer while the component only renders the state. A production implementation would add an &lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt; and clear its timer in the effect cleanup:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEmailVerification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useReducer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;reduceEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"idle"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startVerification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sent"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"error"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Could not start verification"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;retryable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The example leaves polling out on purpose. Polling belongs behind a small adapter that emits &lt;code&gt;matched&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;expired&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;error&lt;/code&gt;; it should not leak timer details into every button and status label. Also, spellings like &lt;code&gt;tamp mail com&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;fake e mail com&lt;/code&gt; may appear in search-driven test input, but they are not valid states or validation rules by themselves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Test transitions instead of screenshots
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reducer tests are quick and tell you more than a large screenshot suite. Cover the happy path, a duplicate event, expiry, and a retryable failure:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ignores a late match after expiry"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"waiting"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"qa@example.test"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduceEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduceEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"matched"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"old-1"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expired"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This style also makes fixtures clearer. A fake inbox can emit a deterministic sequence without pretending to be a browser. The test says what happened and what the UI should show, which is much easier to debug when CI is busy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Q&amp;amp;A: practical tradeoffs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Should every email flow use a state machine?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. A one-shot “send again” form may be fine with local state. Use an explicit union when there are asynchronous steps, retries, expiry, or more than one source of events.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Should the UI poll the inbox directly?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Usually no. Keep provider credentials and matching rules on the server or in a test adapter. The browser needs a safe status event, not the full mailbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What if the backend already has a state machine?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Share event names and IDs where practical, but don't force the frontend to mirror every backend state. Translate server responses into the smaller set of states the user can act on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A shipping checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before merging an email verification screen, check that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every visible state has one &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Late events cannot update a newer attempt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retry and expiry are explicit, not inferred from a timeout alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timers and requests are cleaned up on unmount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tests cover transitions, not only the happy screenshot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test inbox details stay out of browser state and logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Typed contracts are not ceremony for its own sake. They give React a stable boundary around an unreliable async workflow, so the feature is easier to ship, easier to test, and less confusing when email arrives a little late.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kandz Tut’s React Router series breaks down client-side routing across 21 focused parts, from package setup to production server rewrites.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chapter groupings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Parts 01–05 — Foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; installation &amp;amp; dependencies, &lt;code&gt;createBrowserRouter&lt;/code&gt;, route mapping, fallback 404 routes, &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;NavLink&lt;/code&gt; navigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Parts 06–10 — Dynamic &amp;amp; imperative routing:&lt;/strong&gt; active styling, path parameters, query parameters, nested routes with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Outlet&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useNavigate&lt;/code&gt; redirection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Parts 11–15 — Data &amp;amp; mutations:&lt;/strong&gt; route loaders, form actions, pending submission states, fetchers, route-level error boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Parts 16–21 — Advanced &amp;amp; production:&lt;/strong&gt; private route guards, deferred data streaming, lazy loading, testing with &lt;code&gt;createMemoryRouter&lt;/code&gt;, history fallback rewrites, final cheatsheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Router is the standard for routing in React applications. This series covers the full lifecycle — not just basic links — so you can handle nested layouts, data fetching, mutations, and deployment config in one ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who this is for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frontend developers and React learners building single-page apps who need protected routes, dynamic segments, and production-ready server setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read the series&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://tuts.kandz.me/category/programming/frontend-fed/react-ecosystem/react-router/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://tuts.kandz.me/category/programming/frontend-fed/react-ecosystem/react-router/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Which part are you starting with first?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After more than 20 years working with enterprise Data &amp;amp; BI architectures, I've been exploring a different approach to analytical applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What if users could start directly from a semantic model, rather than a predefined report?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This experiment led me to build &lt;strong&gt;PRISM BI&lt;/strong&gt;, an independent conversational analytics application connected to Microsoft Fabric.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwfiyb4ht2g5mxzjye7bj.jpeg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwfiyb4ht2g5mxzjye7bj.jpeg" alt=" " width="800" height="539"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PRISM separates three distinct layers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Semantic layer:&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft Fabric semantic models, including existing measures, dimensions and relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;AI layer:&lt;/strong&gt; interpretation of natural language, analytical planning and DAX query generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Presentation layer:&lt;/strong&gt; a lightweight React-based visualization engine that dynamically renders analytical results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The semantic model remains the foundation of the analytical experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Building a dynamic visualization engine
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The React engine currently supports 14 visualization types, including bar charts, time series, scatter plots, treemaps, heatmaps, donut charts and geographic maps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can change visualization types, interact with data through global cross-filtering, customize colors and reorganize their analytical workspace.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A deterministic 2D packing algorithm evaluates multiple dashboard layouts using visual dimensions, column balance, available space and KPI placement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dashboards, conversations and visual preferences are persisted independently for each semantic model in the authenticated application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


AI where it matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of my main architectural decisions was to avoid using an LLM for operations that can be handled deterministically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Changing visualization types, applying colors or reorganizing a dashboard requires no additional LLM calls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This separation reduces latency, provider dependency and operational costs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Managing AI costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The public demo currently uses GLM-4.7-Flash through Cloudflare Workers AI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PRISM implements budget reservations, token-based cost accounting and automatic reconciliation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During a recent production validation, a revenue-by-country analysis required four LLM calls, with a total metered cost of &lt;strong&gt;$0.000611&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a single measured request, not a general cost benchmark, but it illustrates why usage monitoring and provider selection matter when designing AI-powered applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try the experiment
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The public demo uses an AdventureWorks sample semantic model and requires no registration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://prism.zorveo.xyz/demo" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://prism.zorveo.xyz/demo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The demo has limited AI queries, but users can continue interacting with existing visualizations without consuming additional LLM quota.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Open questions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How far can conversational analytics extend traditional self-service BI?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Which operations genuinely benefit from AI, and which should remain deterministic?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm particularly interested in discussing these architectural trade-offs with developers, Data Engineers and BI architects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disclosure: This article was drafted with AI assistance based on my own development work and production observations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frr6utpyaiqzi7zjstsqk.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frr6utpyaiqzi7zjstsqk.png" alt=" " width="800" height="452"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adding country, state, and city fields to a form often means dealing with large datasets, search functionality, dependent dropdowns, and unnecessary network requests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SonoJS provides a ready-to-use React component to handle all three levels of location selection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Features
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;250+ countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Searchable country, state, and city selectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional country flags&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lazy-loaded location data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loads only the data needed for each selection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designed for forms, checkout flows, and address management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Powered by @sonojs/geo
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component uses &lt;code&gt;@sonojs/geo&lt;/code&gt;, a dedicated geographic data package available independently on npm.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It provides asynchronous APIs for accessing countries, states, and cities, with lazy-loaded data shards, caching, and TypeScript support.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can use it independently in your own JavaScript and TypeScript projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Links
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Component:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://sonojs.com/docs/components/country-city-selector" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://sonojs.com/docs/components/country-city-selector&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;npm:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sonojs/geo" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sonojs/geo&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GitHub:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/SonoJS/SonoJS-geo" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/SonoJS/SonoJS-geo&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Built for the &lt;a href="https://www.kaneclihack.sh/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Kane CLI Hackathon&lt;/a&gt; by TestMu AI.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I found six public repos where the same thing happened. Dependabot opened a React bump. CI went green: type check, lint, build, and in four of them the deploy itself. The PR merged. The live app was a blank page, and the maintainer had to revert it or fix it by hand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of them put it plainly in the revert:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"Format check, lint, typecheck and build stay green, which is why the chain did not catch it."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In all six, the bot raised &lt;code&gt;react&lt;/code&gt; and left &lt;code&gt;react-dom&lt;/code&gt; behind. React refuses to start when the two differ (&lt;a href="https://react.dev/errors/527" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;error #527&lt;/a&gt;), so the bundle throws before the first render. Nothing in a normal CI pipeline opens the app, so nothing sees it. Even npm is happy, because &lt;code&gt;react-dom&lt;/code&gt; only asks for &lt;code&gt;^19&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxpfrab4eiw7rh17zszfv.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxpfrab4eiw7rh17zszfv.jpg" alt="Five public apps: on main each renders; on Dependabot's react bump each page is empty" width="800" height="936"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A green check on a bot PR means the code builds. It doesn't mean checkout still works. So I built &lt;strong&gt;Bumpgate&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  &lt;iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/4M6fN9S-Zgw" width="710" height="399"&gt;
&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On every Dependabot or Renovate PR, Bumpgate:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;builds &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; and the bump side by side (two git worktrees);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has &lt;a href="https://www.testmuai.com/kane-cli/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Kane CLI&lt;/a&gt; replay your app's critical journeys in a real browser on &lt;strong&gt;both&lt;/strong&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;decides with one rule, in plain code: &lt;strong&gt;every journey that passes on main must pass on the bump.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then one of three lights:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🟢 &lt;strong&gt;Green:&lt;/strong&gt; every journey behaves the same. The PR merges itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🟡 &lt;strong&gt;Amber:&lt;/strong&gt; it works, but Kane had to self-heal a step, or new console errors appeared. One human look.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔴 &lt;strong&gt;Red:&lt;/strong&gt; a journey broke. Blocked, and the fix loop starts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A journey is plain English
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No selectors and no page objects. This is a real journey from the demo shop, &lt;code&gt;.kane/checkout_errors_test.md&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gu"&gt;# Checkout explains what is wrong
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## Add a product and go to checkout
&lt;/span&gt;Click "Add to cart" on the first product, click "Cart" in the header, then click "Go to checkout".

&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## Submit with a missing name and a bad email
&lt;/span&gt;Leave "Full name" empty, type "not-an-email" into "Email", then click the "Place order" button.

&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## See the errors
&lt;/span&gt;Verify the message "Please enter your name" is shown.
Verify the message "Enter a valid email address" is shown.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Kane records it once on &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt;, then replays it against each PR build with &lt;code&gt;kane-cli testmd run --override-start-url&lt;/code&gt;. Because the journey describes behaviour, not CSS classes, a UI kit renaming its classes doesn't break it. A checkout that stops showing errors does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Don't want to write them? &lt;code&gt;bumpgate init&lt;/code&gt; has Claude Code draft journeys from your code, and only the drafts Kane passes on &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; are kept.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When something breaks: the closed loop
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a real run, on &lt;a href="https://github.com/Maheswar-Sah00/bumpgatedemo/pull/4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PR #4&lt;/a&gt; in the demo shop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dependabot bumped &lt;code&gt;zod&lt;/code&gt; from 3 to 4. CI passed. Kane ran "Checkout explains what is wrong" on the bump, and the errors never appeared: it failed at step 3, on 2 of 2 runs. Kane's own bug verdict: &lt;em&gt;"Checkout omits required-name validation message (major)"&lt;/em&gt;, with a new console error only on the bump: &lt;code&gt;Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'forEach')&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kane's failed step, reason, bug verdict, console errors and the package's release notes became Claude Code's task. It came back with one line:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-      result.error.errors.forEach((issue) =&amp;gt; {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+      result.error.issues.forEach((issue) =&amp;gt; {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Before anything merges, &lt;strong&gt;code&lt;/strong&gt;, not a prompt, checks the diff. It rejects any fix that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;edits a journey (making the test easier),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;undoes the bump,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;hard-codes a text the journey checks for,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;or is suspiciously large.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then Kane re-runs &lt;strong&gt;every&lt;/strong&gt; journey on the fixed branch: 3 of 3 passed, and it merged. If the fix fails three times, the PR is labelled for a human instead. If you'd rather a person approve every agent-written fix, set &lt;code&gt;merge-fixes: review&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwxih455oap1fix6uvtk3.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwxih455oap1fix6uvtk3.png" alt="Bumpgate's comment on the PR: journeys on base and bump, the failed step, Claude Code's fix, Kane's 3/3 re-run" width="800" height="1600"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Results, with the limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Result&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real React bumps in 6 public repos that passed CI and shipped a blank page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Kane blocks 6 of 6&lt;/strong&gt; at step 1, each failure confirmed by a second run&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Demo shop: zod 3→4 and react-query 4→5 both passed CI and broke the app&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Both blocked, fixed by Claude Code, re-verified by Kane, merged&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Demo shop: clsx 1→2, a safe bump&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Green; merged itself in under 2 minutes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10 open Dependabot PRs in strangers' repos&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2 blank pages (their own CI was red, but a forced install ships them), 1 amber, 7 green&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bot bumps that were merged and never reverted&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;0 false alarms&lt;/strong&gt; on 4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Honest limits:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The six blank pages are &lt;strong&gt;one bug class&lt;/strong&gt;, and I found them by searching for it. 6 of 6 is not a catch rate. A script comparing the two version numbers would catch this one bug too; the point is that one plain-English journey catches it &lt;em&gt;and whatever comes next&lt;/em&gt;, with no rule written for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The app has to run without a private backend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kane runs cost credits (replaying a recorded journey is cheap).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try the whole loop in 10 seconds, no account
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx github:Maheswar-Sah00/bumpgate replay
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It feeds Kane CLI's recorded output from the real PR #4 run through the real gate code: the block, the evidence Claude Code was handed, its fix, the guardrails rejecting two cheating fixes, and Kane's 3/3 re-run. No keys, no credits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Add it to your repo
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight yaml"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# .github/workflows/bumpgate.yml
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;Bumpgate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;pull_request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;types&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;opened&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;synchronize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;reopened&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;permissions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;contents:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;write&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;pull-requests:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;write&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;issues:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;write&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;statuses:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;write&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;jobs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;gate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;github.event.pull_request.user.login == 'dependabot[bot]' || github.event.pull_request.user.login == 'renovate[bot]'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;runs-on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;ubuntu-latest&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;steps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;actions/checkout@v4&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;fetch-depth:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;actions/setup-node@v4&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;node-version:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;Maheswar-Sah00/bumpgate@v1.1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;lt-username&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;${{ secrets.LT_USERNAME }}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;lt-access-key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;${{ secrets.LT_ACCESS_KEY }}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;anthropic-api-key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;One gotcha: Dependabot PRs can only read &lt;strong&gt;Dependabot secrets&lt;/strong&gt;, so add the keys under &lt;em&gt;Settings → Secrets → Dependabot&lt;/em&gt;. And the bump's install scripts never see the TestMu key, the GitHub token or the agent key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why this only works with Kane CLI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The gate needs three things a selector script can't give: a journey that survives cosmetic UI churn but fails on broken behaviour; evidence an agent can act on (the failed step, a bug verdict, console and network); and a re-check of the agent's own fix. Kane is all three: the gate, the evidence, and the referee.&lt;/p&gt;

