&lt;h1&gt;


KaneCLIHackathon #KaneCLI
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi DEV Community! 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm &lt;strong&gt;Houzayfa Zakieh&lt;/strong&gt;, a Computer Engineering student at the University of Aleppo, Frontend Web Developer, and UI Designer. I recently launched my new developer portfolio at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://zakieh.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;zakieh.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to showcase my projects, UI/UX work, and technical journey.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a quick look at what went into building it and how I approach frontend development.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🛠️ The Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For my portfolio, I wanted a setup that is fast, type-safe, and easy to scale as I add new case studies and projects:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Framework:&lt;/strong&gt; Next.js &amp;amp; React.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Language:&lt;/strong&gt; TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Styling:&lt;/strong&gt; Tailwind CSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Feature-Based Architecture to keep components, hooks, and utilities clean and modular&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Custom UI/UX layouts prototyped in Figma before moving to code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🎯 Key Goals Behind the Site
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When designing and building &lt;strong&gt;zakieh.dev&lt;/strong&gt;, I focused on three main things:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Clarity &amp;amp; Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Fast page loads, clean typography, and a distraction-free layout so visitors and recruiters can immediately see what I build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Real-World Projects:&lt;/strong&gt; Highlighting practical applications I've worked on—from multi-role dashboards and management platforms to bilingual (Arabic RTL / English) web interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SEO &amp;amp; Discoverability:&lt;/strong&gt; Setting up proper metadata, semantic HTML, sitemaps, and structured data right from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🚀 What's Next?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now that the first version is live, I plan to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish deeper technical breakdowns of my projects and frontend architecture patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share practical tips on Next.js, TypeScript, and modern UI engineering here on DEV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feel free to check out the live site at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://zakieh.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://zakieh.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;—I’d love to hear your feedback on the design, performance, or structure!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What are you currently building? Drop a link in the comments 👇&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjhz50ljh536kl1mehvtb.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjhz50ljh536kl1mehvtb.png" alt="Screenshot of the Persona 3 Reload-style portfolio main menu with the About, Resume, Socials and Side Projects options" width="800" height="414"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I mostly work on deep learning and computer vision. Frontend isn't my home turf, so building this was a detour, and an enjoyable one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The idea
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two things I like: music and the Persona 3 Reload UI. I kept thinking about how the game's menus feel. Every selection has a sound, a motion, a rhythm. Most portfolios, mine included, are just a page you scroll down. I wanted to see if a portfolio could be something you navigate and interact with instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I built one around that menu.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try it on a laptop:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://persona3.rohitpoul.workers.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://persona3.rohitpoul.workers.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
(Music starts when you enter, so check your volume.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Persona-style menu is the main way you move around&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;About, Resume, Socials and Side Projects each sit behind a menu option&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Looping background music with CD-player controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click and selection sound effects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live GitHub stats pulled into the site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React, Vite and Framer Motion. Framer Motion handles the animated transitions between menu states and sections, which is most of what makes it feel like a game UI and not a webpage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why a menu, not a scroll
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Persona menu works because every action has feedback. Moving the cursor, selecting an option and going back each have a visual and an audio response. I tried to keep that. A portfolio is usually something you skim, but this one gives you a reason to look at each section.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Fan-made, and what I'm releasing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a fan tribute, not affiliated with Atlus or Sega. The source code will be public so anyone can fork it. Assets will only be released where I'm allowed to share them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Repo: &lt;a href="https://github.com/RohitPoul/Person-3-Reload-Potfolio" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/RohitPoul/Person-3-Reload-Potfolio&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Feedback
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you try it, I'd like to know what worked and what didn't, especially on different screen sizes and browsers. A star on the repo helps me decide which side projects deserve more time. And if you were building something like this, what would you add?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most link-in-bio tools feel like they were designed for influencers and social media marketers rather than developers. When you just want one clean place to share your GitHub, side projects, and socials, they often feel cluttered or overly flashy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I built &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://vaultix.lat" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Vaultix&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — a minimal, fast bio link and portfolio hub made specifically for developers and indie builders (&lt;code&gt;vaultix.lat/yourname&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What it does
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;One clean developer URL:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep your projects, socials, and dev identity in a single place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Minimal &amp;amp; distraction-free:&lt;/strong&gt; Designed to put your work first without unnecessary visual bloat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fast setup:&lt;/strong&gt; Create and customize your profile page in seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Tech Stack
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend &amp;amp; Auth:&lt;/strong&gt; Supabase + Auth0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I already have the first few developers using it and setting up their pages, and now I'm focused on refining the experience based on real feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're looking for a clean developer profile page (or just want to test it out and tell me what's missing), check it out at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://vaultix.lat" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;vaultix.lat&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What features do you personally look for in a developer bio/portfolio page?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1.What are Custom Hooks in React?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They are Javascript functions that allows us to reuse stateful logic between multiple React components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React provides built-in-hooks such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useState&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useEffect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useContext&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useReducer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;we can create our own Hooks based on our requriements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important rules:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Custom Hook name should start with use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Custom Hooks can use other React Hooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;They help us reuse logic across components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example of a Custom Hook&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Here:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useCounter is our Custom Hook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useState manages the counter value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;increment increases the count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;decrement decreases the count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We return the count and functions so components can use them.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Here:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useCounter is our Custom Hook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useState manages the counter value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;increment increases the count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;decrement decreases the count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We return the count and functions so components can use them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Using the Custom Hook in a Component&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"./useCounter"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCounter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;decrement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Decrement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We can use the useCounter Hook in other components too. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2.What are Children Props in React?&lt;br&gt;
props.children is a special prop in React that allows a component to receive content placed between its opening and closing tags.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Example:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Welcome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Learning&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;by&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Output&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Welcome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Learning&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;by&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


3.Why do we use Custom Hooks and Children Props?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;**&lt;br&gt;
Custom Hooks:**&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reuse logic between components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce repeated code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep components cleaner and easier to maintain,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Children props:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make components more reusable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allow flexible content inside components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help create reusable layouts,card and containers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I learnt how Custom hooks help us reuse logic across React components and props.children allows us to pass content inside components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;*I recently started learning React.js to improve my frontend development skills and build better web applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As I continue my React learning journey, I learned about two important React Hooks: useMemo and useCallback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;*useMemo: Helps avoid unnecessary recalculations by memoizing values.&lt;br&gt;
*useCallback:Helps prevent unnecessary function recreation by memoizing functions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm continuously learning new concepts and improving my React skills step by step. Looking forward to learning more.&lt;/p&gt;
